args:
- description: |
    A comma-separated list of user IDs to retrieve. Use this to look up users based on their unique identifier in the integrated systems.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: user_id
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: user_id
- description: |
    A comma-separated list of usernames to retrieve. Use this to search for users by their login or account name.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: user_name
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: user_name
- description: |
    A comma-separated list of user email addresses to retrieve. Use this to find users based on their email identifiers
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: user_email
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: user_email
- description: |
    A comma-separated string of specific Active Directory (AD) attributes to retrieve for each user. Only applicable when querying Active Directory based integration.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: attributes
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: attributes
- description: |
    Specifies which integration brand(s) to run the command against. If not set, the command runs across all available integrations. To select multiple integrations, provide a comma-separated list (e.g., "Okta v2,Active Directory Query v2"). Optional values: 'Active Directory Query v2', 'Okta v2', 'AWS - IAM', 'Microsoft Graph User', 'PrismaCloud v2', 'AzureRiskyUsers', 'GSuiteAdmin', 'Cortex XDR - IR', 'Cortex Core - IR'.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: brands
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: brands
- defaultvalue: "true"
  description: |
    If true, returns both risky and non-risky users from Cortex, instead of only risky users. Should be set to "true" unless explicitly scoped to risky users.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: list_non_risky_users
  required: false
  type: boolean
  underlyingargname: list_non_risky_users
- description: |
    Controls the level of detail in the human-readable output. Set to true to return human-readable results from each integration. Set to false to return only the final consolidated result. Optional values: True, False.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: verbose
  required: false
  type: boolean
  underlyingargname: verbose
- defaultvalue: "true"
  description: When set to true, the output will include additional fields about the
    user. Default is true.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: additional_fields
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: additional_fields
